      "rationale": "For a both-changed path, supplies exactly the prescribed native merge result, or uncomputable for conflicted/absent/failed native output. parked_wip_failures compares those expected bytes with the worktree. There is no independent universal parked-added-line retention predicate: a prescribed driver can select or rewrite content. In the named union-catalog missing-row witness, the expected native union result contains that row, so removing it makes equality fail; that witness is not a guarantee for every driver.",
